{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"find .. -name AGENTS.md -print; cat .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md; cat .codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md; cat global_memory_summary.md; jq 'keys' paper_data.json; find source_evidence figures -maxdepth 3 -type f -print; ls -la global_memory/\"","aggregated_output":"../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/vercel/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/supabase-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/data-analytics/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/zoom/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/prototype/AGENTS.md\n../investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/mobile-app/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/vercel/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/supabase-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/data-analytics/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/zoom/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/prototype/AGENTS.md\n../task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261107_045229_1794027149946201781/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/mobile-app/AGENTS.md\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n10. Update distilled conclusions (`conclusions.md`).\n**Purpose.** `conclusions.md` is a *forward-looking guide* for the next worker (or your future self in a later cycle). Its job is to help readers (a) focus their effort on directions you've found promising, and (b) avoid spending compute on directions you've already shown to be unpromising. Each sentence should either point at a lead worth pursuing or warn against a dead end, framed so a researcher who has not read your `memory.md` can still act on it. Avoid chronology, restate-of-results, and post-mortem narration — those belong in `memory.md`. Conclusions are the synthesis layer that makes other workers' next cycles more efficient.\n\n**When.** After every memory-append in the cycle (idea / edit / evaluate / verify / paper / final), evaluate whether `conclusions.md` should be updated.\n\n**Update gate (the only valid triggers).**\n- (a) cycle **contradicts** an existing sentence → rewrite that sentence.\n- (b) cycle opens a **new category** not yet covered → add a sentence.\n- (c) cycle **flips a Do/Don't** recommendation → flip it.\n- (d) cycle **meaningfully refines** an existing sentence — narrows the conditions under which a rule holds, broadens its applicability to a config it wasn't known to apply to, sharpens a tentative claim into a confident one, or adds a qualifier the prior phrasing didn't cover → edit the sentence to incorporate the refinement. Simple re-confirmation in the same regime is **not** sufficient; you must identify the refinement dimension (narrow / broaden / sharpen / qualify) in `--gate-reason`.\n- otherwise → **keep**, do not invoke the helper.\n\n**Format constraints.** Single paragraph. ≤300 words. No blank lines (`\\n\\n`). Avoid detailed numerical figures — use qualitative thresholds (e.g. \"low LR\", \"small batch\") instead of precise floats like `LR=0.205`.\n\n**Update mechanism.** When execution is unavailable, apply the same validation rules\nand update the conclusions files directly with read/edit/write tools. When execution\nis available, use this helper invocation:\n```bash\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" --write-conclusions \\\n  --conclusions-md \"{{CONCLUSIONS_MD_FILE}}\" \\\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl \"{{CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_FILE}}\" \\\n  --cycle-index {{CYCLE_INDEX}} \\\n  --worker-index {{WORKER_INDEX}} \\\n  --gate-trigger <a|b|c|d> \\\n  --gate-reason \"<one sentence; for (d) name the dimension>\" \\\n  --conclusions-text \"<the full new paragraph>\"\n```\n\n**Pre-flight self-check.** Before invoking the helper, count words (`len(paragraph.split())`) and confirm ≤300, and that the paragraph contains no blank line. Most validation rejections can be avoided here.\n\n**Retry budget — exactly 3 attempts per cycle.** On non-zero exit, read the stderr error, shorten the paragraph (drop the least-decisive sentence, merge two related sentences, or remove qualifiers), and retry. After **3 total attempts** with no success, the update is **discarded** for this cycle: do not retry further, do not write the rejected text anywhere, and append a single memory event with `step=\"conclusions_skip\"` whose `summary` names the last validation error. Underlying findings are not lost — they are already durable in `memory.md`.\n\n**Always log the gate decision.** Inside the regular memory append for the cycle, include `gate=<updated|kept|skipped>; trigger=<a|b|c|d|none>; reason=<one sentence>` in the entry's `summary` or `tags`. Use `skipped` only after the 3-attempt budget is exhausted.\n\n# Example evaluation entry\n```markdown\n### 2026-02-13T16:58:00Z | step=evaluate\n- program: program_3\n- combined_score: 2.54\n- correct: true\n- rubrics: uses_restarts=pass, constraint_optimization=pass, score_threshold=fail\n- evidence: late-stage overlap still visible in stdout trace\n- next_recommendation: raise late-stage overlap penalty and diversify restart seeds\n```\n---\nname: retrieve-references\ndescription: Retrieve grounded BibTeX references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (`scholarly`) and write references.bib plus provenance JSON for paper generation.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nFetch references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (via `scholarly`) and keep only real BibTeX entries.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final report/paper generation.\n- Related-work section needs grounded citations.\n\n# What to do\n1. Build focused search queries from task goal, method names, and top experiment ideas.\n2. Preferred path (Semantic Scholar Graph API):\n```bash\npython scripts/s2_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n3. Fallback path (OpenAlex):\n```bash\npython scripts/openalex_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 10 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Optional:\n   - `--mailto you@example.com` to enter the OpenAlex polite pool\n   - Env fallback: `OPENALEX_EMAIL`\n4. Alternate path (Google Scholar API wrapper with `scholarly`):\n```bash\npython -m pip install scholarly\npython scripts/scholarly_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 25 \\\n  --sort-by relevance \\\n  --proxy-mode auto \\\n  --delay-seconds 0.5 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Proxy options:\n   - `--proxy-mode auto|none|free|single`\n   - `--proxy-http <url>` / `--proxy-https <url>` for `single`\n   - Env fallbacks: `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_MODE`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTP`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTPS`\n   - Global `HTTP_PROXY` / `HTTPS_PROXY` are intentionally ignored to avoid accidental ambient proxying\n5. Require `S2_API_KEY` when available for `s2_fetch.py` (script reads env automatically).\n6. Keep only references with valid BibTeX and citation key.\n7. Dedupe by citation key and paper id.\n8. Fail hard if references found `< min-refs`.\n9. Use `s2_fetch.py` first for stability, `openalex_fetch.py` as the next fallback, and `scholarly_fetch.py` last if the other sources fail.\n\n# Outputs\n- `references.bib`\n- `references_provenance.json`\n\n# Notes\n- Use `templates/provenance.schema.json` for expected shape.\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Overlap Aware Target Risk Benchmark Selection; status=idea_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=the cycle supplies a testable proposal but no evaluated finding that changes an evidence-backed recommendation.\n  - evidence: No recent ideas or attempts. Supplied accepted incumbent combined_score=0.9527030000575736, correct=true; its exact named program source path was unavailable. Public matrix structure supports covariance conditioning but no empirical improvement is established. Considered diversity-only selection, unsupported score-adaptive querying, and nonlinear completion; chose a small overlap-shrunk cross-target selector with fixed-target and held-out-family controls. No experiments were run. Only local memory target created or used: ideas/01_overlap_aware_target_risk_benchmark_selection/memory.md.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-07T05:58:37.284239+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: exit=1; cause unavailable; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Score Adaptive Latent Mixture Benchmark Design; status=idea_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=an unexplained execution failure and an untested alternative provide no evidence-backed change to a distilled recommendation.\n  - evidence: Read task/skill documents, supplied histories/manifests/memory/conclusions and prior candidate interface/source only. RPC supplies historical masks, normalized scores, availability and sequential observations; no family labels or outer fixed-target control. Prior exit=1, combined_score=null, correct=false has unknown cause and establishes neither scientific underperformance nor a particular protocol defect. Considered global covariance, one latent Gaussian and raw neighbor kernels; selected a masked latent Gaussian mixture for score-adaptive querying with K=1 and mean fallbacks. No new experiments, numerical probes, installation or task execution. Required JSON rubric arrays reviewed directly; each implementation rubric has executable source_contains patterns. Only local memory target created or used: ideas/02_score_adaptive_latent_mixture_benchmark_design/memory.md.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-07T06:09:49.663879+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: exit=1; cause unavailable; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Saturation Aware Monotone Skill Benchmark Design; status=idea_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=unexplained aggregate execution failures and an untested saturation hypothesis provide no evidence-backed change to distilled recommendations.\n  - evidence: Both recent attempts exited 1 with combined_score=null and correct=false; causes remain unknown. Prior candidate-interface/idea records expose normalized historical scores, masks, availability and sequential observations, not family labels or external fixed-target control. Considered global covariance, latent mixtures and neighbor transfer; selected a shrunk monotone scalar-skill model to test nonlinear saturation with nested task-mean and linear controls. No candidate/evaluator execution, numerical probe or literature lookup. Authored matching rubric arrays reviewed directly; implementation rubrics use 1–8 executable source_contains patterns. Only cycle-local memory target created or used: ideas/03_saturation_aware_monotone_skill_benchmark_design/memory.md.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-07T06:24:36.310628+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: exit=1; cause unavailable; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n[\n  \"ablation_studies\",\n  \"all_programs\",\n  \"best_any\",\n  \"best_correct\",\n  \"downstream_study\",\n  \"evidence_sources\",\n  \"final_evaluation\",\n  \"generated_at\",\n  \"grounding_sources\",\n  \"idea_titles\",\n  \"improvement_trace\",\n  \"paper_profile\",\n  \"presentation_contract\",\n  \"results_dir\",\n  \"top_programs\",\n  \"totals\"\n]\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline/program_spec.toml\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/program_spec.toml\ntotal 164\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 06:26 .\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 06:26 ..\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 05:50 .agent_home\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 05:50 .baseline-seed-6ewnjfck\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 05:50 .hydra\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 05:50 .task-seal-empty\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 06:09 _idea_generation\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  6974 Nov  7 06:24 attempts_history.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   406 Nov  7 05:50 best_program_manifest.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    22 Nov  7 05:50 conclusions.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     0 Nov  7 06:26 conclusions_history.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    41 Nov  7 05:50 conclusions_other_workers.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 60417 Nov  7 06:24 events.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     0 Nov  7 05:50 idea_generation_failures.jsonl\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 06:13 ideas\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 12152 Nov  7 06:13 ideas_history.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   724 Nov  7 06:13 latest_run_manifest.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 10662 Nov  7 06:24 memory.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 11696 Nov  7 06:24 memory.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   545 Nov  7 06:24 outer_state.json\ndrwxrwxr-x 3 agent agent  4096 Nov  7 05:50 task\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
