"final.evidence.episodes\",\n    \"final.metric.combined_score\",\n    \"final.metric.constant_score\",\n    \"final.metric.control_failure_fraction\",\n    \"final.metric.copy_score\",\n    \"final.metric.correct\",\n    \"final.metric.corruption_gap\",\n    \"final.metric.failed_episode_fraction\",\n    \"final.metric.medoid_ridge_score\",\n    \"final.metric.mteb_score\",\n    \"final.metric.open_llm_score\",\n    \"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\",\n    \"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\",\n    \"final.metric.permuted_score\",\n    \"final.metric.random_lowrank_score\",\n    \"final.metric.reset_replay_ok\",\n    \"final.metric.selected_ridge_score\",\n    \"final.qualification.correct\",\n    \"final.qualification.outcome\",\n    \"final.qualification.status\",\n    \"result.total_attempts\",\n    \"result.total_correct_programs\",\n    \"result.total_evaluated_programs\",\n    \"result.total_ideas\",\n    \"study.attempts.scored\",\n    \"study.attempts.total\",\n    \"study.attempts.unscored\",\n    \"study.baseline_score\",\n    \"study.final.correct\",\n    \"study.final.outcome\",\n    \"study.final.status\",\n    \"study.investigation_outcome\",\n    \"study.search_score\",\n    \"study.search_score_delta\",\n    \"study.selection_kind\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"attempt_counts\": {\n    \"scored\": 0,\n    \"total\": 3,\n    \"unscored\": 3\n  },\n  \"baseline_program_dir\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261107_045228/investigation/.baseline-seed-6ewnjfck/program_0\",\n  \"baseline_score\": 0.9527030000575736,\n  \"baseline_tree_sha256\": \"33fc15401729399a8a88a6f041ce38f1279d47925bd6d123e805fb82ff752560\",\n  \"combined_score\": 0.9527030000575736,\n  \"entrypoint_path\": \"src/program.py\",\n  \"final_evaluation\": {\n    \"correct\": true,\n    \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\"\n  },\n  \"investigation_outcome\": \"completed_no_winner\",\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Investigation found no qualifying winner; selection used search evidence only.\",\n    \"Unscored attempts are missing performance evidence, not measured losses.\",\n    \"Search scores and sealed final metrics belong to different evaluation scopes.\",\n    \"An unqualified final outcome may reflect validity or other criteria; do not infer that failure means only an inferior score. Interpret metrics within those limitations.\"\n  ],\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261107_045228/downstream/program\",\n  \"program_tree_sha256\": \"33fc15401729399a8a88a6f041ce38f1279d47925bd6d123e805fb82ff752560\",\n  \"search_score_delta\": 0.0,\n  \"selection_kind\": \"baseline\",\n  \"source_attempt_id\": \"bootstrap\",\n  \"source_evidence\": {\n    \"baseline\": \"source_evidence/downstream/baseline\",\n    \"program\": \"source_evidence/downstream/program\"\n  },\n  \"source_program_dir\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261107_045228/investigation/.baseline-seed-6ewnjfck/program_0\",\n  \"source_tree_sha256\": \"33fc15401729399a8a88a6f041ce38f1279d47925bd6d123e805fb82ff752560\"\n}\n---\nname: retrieve-references\ndescription: Retrieve grounded BibTeX references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (`scholarly`) and write references.bib plus provenance JSON for paper generation.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nFetch references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (via `scholarly`) and keep only real BibTeX entries.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final report/paper generation.\n- Related-work section needs grounded citations.\n\n# What to do\n1. Build focused search queries from task goal, method names, and top experiment ideas.\n2. Preferred path (Semantic Scholar Graph API):\n```bash\npython scripts/s2_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n3. Fallback path (OpenAlex):\n```bash\npython scripts/openalex_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 10 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Optional:\n   - `--mailto you@example.com` to enter the OpenAlex polite pool\n   - Env fallback: `OPENALEX_EMAIL`\n4. Alternate path (Google Scholar API wrapper with `scholarly`):\n```bash\npython -m pip install scholarly\npython scripts/scholarly_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 25 \\\n  --sort-by relevance \\\n  --proxy-mode auto \\\n  --delay-seconds 0.5 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Proxy options:\n   - `--proxy-mode auto|none|free|single`\n   - `--proxy-http <url>` / `--proxy-https <url>` for `single`\n   - Env fallbacks: `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_MODE`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTP`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTPS`\n   - Global `HTTP_PROXY` / `HTTPS_PROXY` are intentionally ignored to avoid accidental ambient proxying\n5. Require `S2_API_KEY` when available for `s2_fetch.py` (script reads env automatically).\n6. Keep only references with valid BibTeX and citation key.\n7. Dedupe by citation key and paper id.\n8. Fail hard if references found `< min-refs`.\n9. Use `s2_fetch.py` first for stability, `openalex_fetch.py` as the next fallback, and `scholarly_fetch.py` last if the other sources fail.\n\n# Outputs\n- `references.bib`\n- `references_provenance.json`\n\n# Notes\n- Use `templates/provenance.schema.json` for expected shape.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
